course: dictionary
lesson: 10960
title: Finding the right meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means. Wallow can be an action or a place. «Rhinos wallow in mud, which cools them and protects their skin from sunburn and biting flies.» The mud and the cooling clues tell you wallow means to roll about in mud to cool down.
explain: Wallow can also describe a feeling. People talk about «wallowing in self-pity» when they stay miserable instead of trying to feel better. The words self-pity and miserable are the clues: this meaning is about being sad for a long time, not about mud.
explain: Always check by swapping in your meaning. Does «Pigs roll about in mud to keep cool» still make sense? Yes, so that meaning fits. Try the other meaning in the same place and see if it still sounds right. If it does not, you have found the right one.
fact: Wallow means to roll about in mud or water to cool down.
fact: Wallow can also mean to let yourself stay sad or upset for a long time and enjoy feeling sorry for yourself.
fact: «Pigs wallow in mud to keep cool, because they cannot sweat much.»
fact: A wallow can also be a noun: a muddy place where animals roll about.
fact: Phrases to know: wallow in mud, and wallow in self-pity.
exercise: «Pigs wallow in mud to keep cool.» What does wallow mean here? | *To roll about in mud to cool down | To sing loudly for a crowd | To sleep under a tree all afternoon | To run very fast to school
exercise: Dad says, «The buffalo found a wallow near the river.» What is a wallow here? | A loud noise in the night | A fast boat on the river | *A muddy place where animals roll about | A kind of tall tree
exercise: Tom says, «I lost the match, so I am wallowing in self-pity.» What does wallowing in self-pity mean? | Practising football very hard | Splashing happily in a pool | *Staying upset and feeling sorry for yourself | Making a big meal for friends
test: «Rhinos wallow in mud, which protects their skin from sunburn.» Why do rhinos wallow in mud? | To find food in the river | *To keep cool and protect their skin | To show they are angry | To practise swimming
test: Ella writes, «She wallowed in the sad book all evening and cried.» Which meaning fits best? | To walk slowly up a hill | *To stay sad for a long time and enjoy the feeling | To give out a bright light | To roll about in mud to cool down
exam: Which meaning of wallow fits «Hippos wallow in the river on hot days»? | *To roll about in mud or water to cool down | A muddy place where animals roll about | To let yourself feel sorry for yourself | To enjoy a sweet snack very much
